  "notes": "{増|ま}す is a godan verb meaning \"to increase\" or \"to grow.\" Can be transitive or intransitive.\n\nTRANSITIVITY:\n- Can be both transitive and intransitive\n- Compare: {増|ふ}える (intransitive), {増|ふ}やす (transitive) - more common in everyday speech\n\nCOMMON COLLOCATIONS:\n- {勢|いきお}いを{増|ま}す: to gain momentum\n- {重要性|じゅうようせい}を{増|ま}す: to grow in importance\n- {速度|そくど}を{増|ま}す: to increase speed\n- {輝|かがや}きを{増|ま}す: to shine more brightly\n\nREGISTER:\n{増|ま}す is more literary/formal than {増|ふ}える. Common in written language and news.\n\nRELATED:\n- {減|へ}る: to decrease (opposite)\n- ますます: more and more, increasingly",
